# Line endings and file types.
#
# The repository stores every text file with LF. Without this file the checked-out
# form depends on each machine's core.autocrlf, so a clone with a different setting
# produces spurious whole-file diffs.
#
# All sources are ASCII, or UTF-8 without a BOM. Do not add a BOM to accommodate
# Windows PowerShell 5.1: its Get-Content falls back to the ANSI code page for
# BOM-less files and misreads the Chinese documents, while every compiler, editor
# and Git itself read UTF-8 correctly.

# Text files are normalised to LF on commit and checked out as LF, so the working
# tree no longer depends on core.autocrlf.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never normalise, never treat as text. A file git's content sniffing
# mistook for text would be corrupted by end-of-line translation.
*.spv    binary
*.dll    binary
*.exe    binary
*.lib    binary
*.a      binary
*.o      binary
*.pdb    binary

# Images and binary model containers. The text siblings (*.gltf, *.obj as a
# Wavefront model) are deliberately not listed: text=auto classifies them by
# content, and *.obj is ambiguous with a compiler object file.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.bmp    binary
*.tga    binary
*.dds    binary
*.ktx    binary
*.ktx2   binary
*.glb    binary
*.fbx    binary
*.zip    binary
*.7z     binary
*.gz     binary
